.TH AIO_SUSPEND 3 "July 2026" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
aio_suspend, aio_error, aio_return, aio_cancel, lio_listio \- await and
inspect asynchronous I/O
.SH LIBRARY
Realtime library (librt, \-lrt)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <aio.h>
.PP
.BI "int aio_suspend(const struct aiocb *const " list "[], int " nent ", const struct timespec *" timeout );
.br
.BI "int aio_error(const struct aiocb *" aiocbp );
.br
.BI "ssize_t aio_return(struct aiocb *" aiocbp );
.br
.BI "int aio_cancel(int " fildes ", struct aiocb *" aiocbp );
.br
.BI "int lio_listio(int " mode ", struct aiocb *const " list "[], int " nent ", struct sigevent *" sig );
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR aio_suspend ()
blocks the calling thread until at least one of the
.I nent
requests in
.I list
completes, until a signal is delivered, or (if
.I timeout
is non-NULL) until the relative time interval
.RB * timeout
elapses.  NULL entries in
.I list
are ignored.
.PP
.BR aio_error ()
returns the error status of the request
.RB * aiocbp :
.B EINPROGRESS
if the request has not completed, 0 if it completed successfully,
.B ECANCELED
if it was cancelled, or the
.I errno
of the failed underlying operation.
.PP
.BR aio_return ()
returns the final return value of a
.I completed
request \(em the byte count that the equivalent synchronous
.BR pread (2)/ pwrite (2)
would have returned, or \-1 on failure \(em and then releases the internal
state associated with the request.  It must be called exactly once per
completed request and only after
.BR aio_error ()
reports something other than
.BR EINPROGRESS .
.PP
.BR aio_cancel ()
attempts to cancel outstanding requests for
.IR fildes .
If
.I aiocbp
is non-NULL only that request is considered; otherwise all requests for the
descriptor are.  Requests that have not yet started are cancelled; requests
already running to completion cannot be interrupted.
.PP
.BR lio_listio ()
submits the list of
.I nent
requests, each with
.I aio_lio_opcode
set to
.BR LIO_READ ,
.BR LIO_WRITE ,
or
.BR LIO_NOP .
If
.I mode
is
.BR LIO_WAIT ,
the call blocks until all operations complete.  If
.I mode
is
.BR LIO_NOWAIT ,
the call returns immediately and, when every operation has completed, the
notification in
.RB * sig
(if non-NULL) is delivered.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR aio_suspend ()
returns 0 if a request completed, or \-1 with
.I errno
set to
.B EAGAIN
on timeout or
.B EINTR
on a signal.
.BR aio_error ()
returns an error number (or 0), or \-1 on a bad control block.
.BR aio_return ()
returns the request's return value, or \-1.
.BR aio_cancel ()
returns
.BR AIO_CANCELED ,
.BR AIO_NOTCANCELED ,
or
.BR AIO_ALLDONE .
.BR lio_listio ()
returns 0 on success or \-1 on error.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EAGAIN
.RB ( aio_suspend )
The timeout elapsed before any request completed.
.TP
.B EINTR
.RB ( aio_suspend )
A signal interrupted the wait.
.TP
.B EINVAL
A control block pointer is invalid, or
.RB ( lio_listio )
.I mode
is neither
.B LIO_WAIT
nor
.BR LIO_NOWAIT .
.TP
.B EINPROGRESS
.RB ( aio_return )
The request has not yet completed.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
struct aiocb a, b;
/* ... fill in a and b with LIO_WRITE opcodes ... */
struct aiocb *l[2] = { &a, &b };
lio_listio(LIO_WAIT, l, 2, NULL);   /* submit both, wait for completion */
printf("a=%zd b=%zd\\n", aio_return(&a), aio_return(&b));
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aio_read (3),
.BR aio_write (3)
